{"n": 105, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "105.webp", "text": "All Models:\n\nLoosen bolts (7 and 8).\nPress in tensioning roller.\nTighten bolt (8).\n\nTake toothed drive belt off of camshaft\n\nNever crank engine after removing belt.\nInstallation:\n\nAlways replace an used belt after loosening\nthe tensioning roller, regardless of the\nmileage***\n\nReplace toothed drive belt — see 11 31 110.\n\nInstallation:\n\nTurn in camshaft prior to mounting the\ncylinder head in such a manner, that mark on\ncamshaft sprocket points to mark on cylinder\nhead.\n\nCylinder no. 1 is at TOC.\n\nAlso install toothed drive belt in this position.\n\n*** See Service Information of Gr, 11\n\nSaal 2019036\n\nUnscrew bolts mn order of 14 through 1 and\ntake off cylinder head.\n\nInstallation:\n\nKeep oil out of cavities, since otherwise bolts\ntightened with specified torque might not\nexert sufficient force on the cylinder head.\n\nIn addition, the crankcase could be cracked.\nClean cylinder head bolts.\n\nLubricate threads and bearing surfaces of bolt\nheads with oil lightly.\n\nReplace cylinder head gasket see 11.12 101\n\nTighten bolts in order of 1 through 14 in three\nsteps.\n\nTightening torque*.\n\nAdjust valve clearance - see 11 34 004\nAdjust ignition timing — see 12 11 004,\nAdjust engine idle speed and CO level — see\n13 00 054,\n\nIn the 3rd step (cylinder head cover removed\nagain after running engine warm) tighten the\ncylinder head bolts to specified torque angle\nwith Special Tool 11 2 110 regardless of the\nengine temperature.\n\nNote:\n\nCylinder head does not have to be tightened\nafter 1,000 km (600 miles).\n\n* See Specifications", "words": [["All", 0.2604, 0.0716, 0.2736, 0.0816], ["Models:", 0.2781, 0.0716, 0.3146, 0.0822], ["Loosen", 0.2609, 0.0875, 0.2948, 0.0981], ["bolts", 0.2989, 0.0875, 0.3217, 0.0975], ["(7", 0.3257, 0.0875, 0.3343, 0.0981], ["and", 0.3384, 0.0875, 0.3546, 0.0975], ["8).", 0.3587, 0.0875, 0.3708, 0.0981], ["Press", 0.2604, 0.1028, 0.2837, 0.